BT /F2 15 Tf 72 730 Td (Jackson Creek Vegetation Restoration - Scoping Letter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL 72 700 Td
(USDA Forest Service - Cleveland National Forest - Descanso Ranger District) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(August 3, 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dear Interested Party,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Descanso Ranger District is proposing the Jackson Creek Vegetation Restoration) Tj T*
(project on approximately 1,250 acres of National Forest System lands in the Jackson) Tj T*
(Creek drainage, San Diego County, California \(T15S R4E, Sections 10, 11, 14 and 15,) Tj T*
(SBBM\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Purpose and need: decades of fire exclusion have allowed dense, decadent chamise) Tj T*
(chaparral to encroach on coast live oak woodland, increasing fuel continuity near the) Tj T*
(community of Descanso. Non-native tamarisk and giant reed are displacing native riparian) Tj T*
(vegetation along Jackson Creek.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Proposed action: masticate decadent chaparral in units JC-01 and JC-02 \(about 333) Tj T*
(acres\); hand-thin and pile brush around oaks in unit JC-03 \(about 82 acres\); manually) Tj T*
(remove invasive plants along the riparian corridor in unit JC-04 \(about 88 acres\). No) Tj T*
(herbicides and no new road construction are proposed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We anticipate documenting this decision with a Categorical Exclusion under 36 CFR) Tj T*
(220.6\(e\)\(6\), timber stand and/or wildlife habitat improvement activities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Please send comments by September 8, 2026. A public open house will be held on August) Tj T*
(20, 2026 at the Descanso Community Hall.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Sincerely, District Ranger, Descanso Ranger District) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
